<p>
  Every business tracks something special: a customer's tier, a contract renewal date, the
  number of employees. Custom fields add those to Zippiker without any setup work.
</p>

<h2>Adding a field</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Admins open <.link navigate="/settings/custom-fields">Settings → Custom fields</.link>.</li>
  <li>
    Choose what it belongs to: contacts, companies, leads, deals, products, quotes or invoices.
  </li>
  <li>Give it a label and a type, and mark it required if every record must have it.</li>
</ol>
<p>The field appears on that kind of record's form and page right away.</p>

<h2>Field types</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Type</th><th>Good for</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Short / long text</td><td>Reference codes, notes</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Number</td><td>Employees, seats, square meters</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Date</td><td>Contract renewal, birthday</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Yes / no</td><td>Newsletter opt-in, VIP</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Dropdown</td><td>Tier, region, industry</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Multi-select</td><td>Interests, products used</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>URL, Email</td><td>LinkedIn profile, accounts contact (checked for a valid format)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Filtering</h2>
<p>
  Dropdown, multi-select and yes/no fields become filters on the list pages for contacts,
  companies, leads and products. Pick a value to see only the matching records.
</p>
<.callout>
  Renaming a field or adding options is safe: existing values are kept.
</.callout>
